00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:40.180
episode

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:40.180
"Before

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:40.180
the Door of Fate''

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.630
I'm sure you're all aware by now.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.080
Company B will advance to Paris'
Tuileries Square at 8 in the morning.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.750
Our mission is to keep the armed
demonstrators in check,

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.800
but if it turns into a riot, we must open fire
at the demonstrators and suppress the riot.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.920
Please continue.

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:29.020
I'm aware your parents and
siblings may be among the crowd.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:36.880
Even if I order you to open fire,
I doubt you'll pull the trigger.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.400
How could you, after all?

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.450
Let me tell you what I think...

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.420
No, let me tell you what path I feel I should take.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.220
This is solely my personal decision.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.510
I hereby...

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.250
...resign as your commander,

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.510
because...

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.970
...I know the man I love and trust,

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:09.200
wouldn't open fire at the people,
just like the rest of you.

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:11.810
I will follow his decision.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:16.240
If he wishes to fight with the people,
I'll fight alongside them, as well.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.010
Guardsmen...

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.740
I've become André Grandier's wife.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:26.610
My wish is to become a wife who walks with
her husband and the path he believes in.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:29.790
Oscar...

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.240
Tell me, André.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.840
The path you choose is the
path I'll trust and follow.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:47.800
Commander, there's no need for you to resign.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:50.510
We discussed it before you came.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:57.850
If a battle begins, we've agreed to quit the French
Guards on the spot, and join the revolution!

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.820
But if that's how you feel, we won't have to do that.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.450
We'll fight with the people under your command!

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.080
Instead of fighting separately, we'll be
much more useful as a unit!

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:09.780
André...

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.080
Alain is right, Oscar.

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:17.880
Commander!

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.800
Commander!

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:20.800
Commander!

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.800
Commander!

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:20.800
Commander!

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:20.800
Commander!

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:20.800
Commander!

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.080
We're counting on you, Commander.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.890
And congratulations to the both of you.

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:32.980
Thank you...

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.500
Colonel d'Agout.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:43.470
Yes!

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:44.870
You're a noble.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.610
I doubt you'll join us.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.110
No, I'm afraid I can't.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:55.610
You are free to report what you've just
heard to the Regiment Command Center.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:57.580
Yes, I intend to report it.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:58.550
What?!

00:05:58.550 --> 00:05:59.350
However—

00:05:58.980 --> 00:05:59.880
Wait!

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.540
Let the man finish.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:06.020
However, I plan to be absent without leave today.

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:09.160
Therefore, I won't be able to make
my report until after tomorrow.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.300
Please take care of yourself.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.810
Colonel d'Agout...

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:24.510
I always thought he was just an
uptight, hard-headed man, but...

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.000
Thank you, Colonel.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.390
All right, Guardsmen!

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:51.550
Move out!

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.730
Let's go, everyone!

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.690
Yeah!

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:26.000
Paris - 8 A.M.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:40.310
Tuileries Square

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:45.220
Just where did they get those guns from?!

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:47.360
Only a fraction of them had guns yesterday.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:52.820
Last night, the armory of the Invalides was
raided and 23,000 guns were seized by them.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.410
Hey, Royal Lapdogs! Listen up!

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:59.840
We've got guns, too!

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:02.370
Move out of the way, or you're
going to get seriously hurt!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.670
Move it, Tax Thieves!

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.780
Go back to your own country!

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.810
Darling, cut it out already!

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:11.420
There's no point in angering the soldiers!

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.150
Yeah, I guess so...

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:15.840
Damn bastards!

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.560
M-Michel...!

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.030
Michel!

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.500
Michel!

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:44.170
Get them!

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.890
Fire, fire, fire!

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:10.270
<i>On July 13, 1789,</i>

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:15.750
<i>a lone soldier's gunshot had finally triggered
the start of the French Revolution,</i>

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:20.480
<i>where ghastly battles and bloodshed
were retaliated with blood.</i>

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.190
Commander!

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:27.550
Commander Oscar!

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:30.000
The army has begun to open fire on the people!

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:35.500
Paris is now a battlefield!

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:38.600
The military is attacking indiscriminately,
even against those who are unarmed!

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:41.000
Tuileries Square is now a pool a blood!

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:42.610
Don't let them get away!

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:44.310
Fire! Fire! Fire!

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:51.860
<i>Although they were armed, the people
weren't organized as a force.</i>

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:57.680
<i>They stood no chance head on, against
the overwhelming firepower of the military.</i>

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:00.410
Everyone! Retreat for now!

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.280
Don't become a casualty!

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.530
Rosalie, are you hurt anywhere?

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:09.300
I'm fine, Bernard.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:10.100
Let's go.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:16.500
It's the French Guards!

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:19.580
The French Guards have us blocked!

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:21.050
Why you...!

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:22.480
Wait!

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:24.520
We do not wish to fight you.

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:26.720
You don't want to fight us?

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:28.100
What do you mean by that?

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:32.310
If we did, we would have opened
fire as you retreated.

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:35.030
W-Well, I guess that's true...

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:37.950
Anyhow, please let us through.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:41.910
Hey, everyone! They said they
want to pass through!

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.340
Lady Oscar...

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.720
I take it that you're the
French Guards Company B?!

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.440
I'm Lambesc, Commander of
the German Cavalry Regiment!

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:15.820
State your title and rank.

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:18.040
I am Oscar François.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:20.400
However, I have no title or rank!

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:52.220
Please withdraw your soldiers, Duke Lambesc.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:55.280
Or else, we'll open fire on you and your men.

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:57.240
Wh-What is the meaning of this...?

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:02.780
We, French Guards Company B
have defected, as of today.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:03.780
What?!

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.160
There you have it!

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:07.100
Well, are you going to withdraw or not?!

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.240
Hurry up and answer!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.930
E-Everyone, retreat!

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:28.430
I won't be needing this rank insignia anymore.

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:35.810
Oscar!

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:50.540
Does this mean you're willing to fight with us?

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:52.580
Indeed, we are.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:56.380
We can't trust you! How could we?

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:59.040
You didn't fire a single bullet at them just now!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.650
Yeah!

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:03.920
You're only trying to join us, so you
can fire at us from behind!

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:06.510
All we know for sure is that these
guys were the Queen's lapdogs!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.690
Yeah, we can't trust them.

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:08.760
Listen to yourselves!

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.470
H-How could you say that?! We're...!

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.430
My God...

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:17.540
Listen, it's true we received our
pay from the royal household,

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:19.400
but that doesn't mean we sold our souls!

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:21.660
Stay back!

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:24.640
Soldiers are the last thing we're going to trust!

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:25.580
C-Commander!

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:28.750
Their concerns are completely understandable.

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:31.330
It seems we were naïve in our thinking.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:32.830
Even so,

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:36.350
we need to earn their trust no matter what.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:38.120
Alain, hold on to these.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:40.340
Oscar!

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:54.350
Please hear me out!

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:57.060
I used to be noble.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:04.230
I have no right to protest, if you wish to shoot
and kill me here for that reason alone.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:08.360
But please believe my words!

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:13.960
These guardsmen with me urged me to
do this and they are different from me!

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:17.670
They are from the Third Estate and possess
the same conviction as all of you!

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:23.130
Although these men received their pay from the French Guards,
they have been eagerly waiting for this day to come!

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:27.100
Please, at least trust my men!

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:30.560
Please trust them and fight with them!

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:34.730
In return, I'm willing to be shot dead here!

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:51.660
Bernard.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.120
I'll trust the French Guards.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.870
And you, as well.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:58.630
Welcome, Oscar François.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.580
Thank you, Bernard Châtelet.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.640
Hey, that's Monsieur Robespierre's protégé.

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:06.840
You're right. It's Bernard Châtelet.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:09.250
If Bernard is going to trust them...
then maybe we can, too.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:11.550
Yeah, we can trust them.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:20.940
Hey, let's do this together!

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:23.520
Y-Yeah, let's do it!

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:24.660
Pleased to meet you!

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:25.690
Same here!

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:32.950
I had a feeling this day would
eventually come, André.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:34.340
Bernard.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:36.800
Glad to have you onboard. Let's do this!

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:42.980
Rosalie!

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:03.310
About 500 soldiers of the Allemand Regiment
are headed towards this way!

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:11.480
Former French Guardsmen!

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:12.910
All mount!

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:14.410
{This is w}What we've been waiting for!

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:22.650
Wait, Oscar!

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:23.720
What are you going to do?!

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:27.420
We'll carry out a preemptive strike
and stop their advance.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:31.380
In the meantime, build a barricade in this square.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:33.090
A barricade?

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:34.200
Yes.

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:37.800
If you build a barricade, you'll be able fight on
par with the military with limited weapons.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:38.670
All right?

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:40.200
I see. Understood.

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:41.100
All right then.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.270
All advance!

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.110
Listen closely!

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:17.940
Once we catch them off guard and
attract their attention towards us,

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:20.040
head towards the opposite direction of the square!

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:23.350
Make them follow us and distance
them from the square!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:25.810
All right! Charge into their flank!

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.680
Enemy attack!

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.160
It's the French Guards who have defected!

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:40.600
Keep your positions!

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:00.070
Why you...!

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:02.120
André, what's wrong?!

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.380
Get it together!

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:05.160
Alain!

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:06.190
I can't...!

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:07.180
My eye...!

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:11.030
It's not just blurry! It's becoming darker and darker!

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:12.330
André!

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:14.990
Of all timings, too!

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:22.140
All right!

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:23.580
Everyone, retreat!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:24.790
You got it!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.500
All right!

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:29.920
Come on, out of the way!

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:35.990
Don't let them get away!

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.890
Fire! Fire away!

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:44.810
André, keep your head down!

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:07.480
Word has just come in.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:11.220
Fifty men led by Oscar François have passed
Canal Saint-Martin and are headed this way.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:15.800
July 13th - 3 P.M.

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:18.500
<i>By the afternoon, the clash between the military
and people had spread throughout the city,</i>

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:21.660
<i>and the level of violence continued to escalate.</i>

00:19:28.340 --> 00:19:32.930
<i>Furthermore, the order from the Regiment Command
Center to kill off the former French Guardsmen,</i>

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:35.780
<i>had already been relayed to all the regiments.</i>

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:41.860
They're coming!

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:46.330
Fire!

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:03.010
Retreat! Retreat! Retreat!

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:06.540
After them!

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:07.560
Kill them all!

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:29.170
Lazare!

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:30.030
Come back!

00:20:56.860 --> 00:21:00.160
<i>The 50 Guardsmen had been
reduced to roughly half.</i>

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:07.740
At any rate, we need to return to Tuileries Square.

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:12.710
With so few of us left, the only way for us
to fight is to join Bernard and his group.

